"""Hiking trail: a chain of plain waypoints from trailhead to summit.

The waypoints carry no payload — they're just nodes on the path. A hiker
walker traverses them, prints each stop number as it goes, and emits a
completion line once enough waypoints have been passed.
"""

node Waypoint {
    has label: str = "";
}

walker Hiker {
    has stop_count: int = 0;
    has target_stops: int = 5;

    can start with Root entry {
        print("Hiker begins the ascent");
        visit [-->] else { disengage; }
    }

