Models the essential scenario from issue #146: a release-facing claim system
that ties each public claim to its evidence artifact, epistemic level, and
invalidator list, then walks the graph to flag any wording that exceeds what
its source evidence actually supports (e.g. "bound"/"certified" prose whose
underlying endpoint_resolutions_applied count is zero).
